# From https://www.reddit.com/r/emulation/comments/8w1lqd/comment/e1ryp97/
#
#     RetroArch has now gained a Metal renderer! Targeting modern macOS at first. XMB/MaterialUI works, menu shader pipelines work, Slang shaders work thanks to SPIRV-Cross, fonts work, etc!
#
#     Previously, RetroArch for OSX/macOS only had an OpenGL video driver. Since Apple will be deprecating OpenGL support in the near future, this Metal video driver essentially future proofs RetroArch for mac!﻿
#
# So, let's go with Metal instead of OpenGL.

# Update from 2026-10-17:
#
# RetroArch 1.22.2, the latest stable version at time of writing, is very laggy on macOS Ventura 13. It relates to these bugs:
#
# https://github.com/libretro/RetroArch/issues/18674
# https://github.com/libretro/RetroArch/issues/18408
# https://github.com/libretro/RetroArch/issues/18417
#
# The Nightly version at time of writing works well, however, so we need to use it.
cask 'retroarch-metal@nightly'

# Dolphin has a Metal renderer. Sadly, this renderer is not supported by the Dolphin libretro core and the gl, glcore, and vulkan video drivers do not result in playable games.
#
# See where the Metal video backend is excluded from the build here: https://github.com/libretro/dolphin/blob/71fd149aa682cf7b78c4fbd23e5b0896510e57dd/Source/Core/VideoBackends/CMakeLists.txt#L11
#
# This seems to be the best issue tracking the lack of Metal: https://github.com/libretro/dolphin/issues/344
#
# The end result is that GameCube games must be played in Dolphin standalone, at least for now.
cask 'dolphin'

